KaTeX v0.18.5
Source: https://github.com/KaTeX/KaTeX/releases/tag/v0.18.5
Release asset: katex.tar.gz
Release tarball sha256: a4122a3f8879fd2b9db5de6a8f19113b2287ab305ee20ed9ca60bd9caf8ae369

Vendored here, not fetched at deploy time -- unlike scripts/fetch-privacy-filter.sh
(~920 MB, has to live outside git), this whole runtime is ~600 KB, small enough to
commit directly. Same posture as app/protect.py: vendored, provenance recorded here
instead of re-derived.

What's kept, out of the full release tarball:
  katex.min.js, katex.min.css, contrib/auto-render.min.js
  fonts/*.woff2 only -- woff/ttf fallbacks dropped. Every browser this app targets
  (Safari/iPadOS, Chrome) supports woff2, and a browser skips a @font-face `src`
  entry its format() hint says it can't use, so the woff/ttf entries still present
  in katex.min.css never fire a request even though those files aren't here.

To update: download the new release's katex.tar.gz, verify its sha256, and repeat
the same copy. Do not hand-edit anything under this directory.
